From c1307b9325632282510e67b809624a77360312c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:06:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 058/165] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: Feed the USB3 PHY pipe
 clock to GCC

The last GCC clock input, DT_USB3_PHY_WRAPPER_GCC_USB30_PIPE_CLK, was
left as <0>, so gcc_usb3_prim_phy_pipe_clk_src was an orphan running at
0 Hz while the QMP PHY's pipe clock had no consumer. Wire it to the
USB/DP PHY like sm8750 does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 21380d32fe0f..ac54c625926a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -551,7 +551,7 @@ gcc: clock-controller@100000 {
 				 <&ufs_mem_phy 0>,
 				 <&ufs_mem_phy 1>,
 				 <&ufs_mem_phy 2>,
-				 <0>;
+				 <&usb_dp_qmpphy QMP_USB43DP_USB3_PIPE_CLK>;
 
 			power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_CX>;
 
-- 
2.56.0

